{"name":"Alien Breed","hex":"#b9cc81","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alien","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person, animal, plant, or other thing which is from outside the family, group, organization, or territory under consideration.","A citizen or national of another sovereign state."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not belonging to the same country, land, or government, or to the citizens or subjects thereof; foreign.","Very unfamiliar, strange, or removed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien"},{"term":"breed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce offspring sexually; to bear young.","To give birth to; to be the native place of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["All animals or plants of the same species or subspecies.","A race or lineage; offspring or issue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alien Breed","blocks":[{"text":"Alien Breed is a series of top-down science fiction shoot 'em up video games developed by Team17 primarily for the Amiga in the 1990s, heavily inspired by the Alien films and featuring game play reminiscent of the classic arcade game Gauntlet. Later, first-person shooter titles were released under the Alien Breed name. In 2009, the series was revived with Alien Breed Evolution."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Breed","wikidata":"Q2267429"},{"title":"Alien Breed (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Alien Breed is a top down run and gun video game released in 1991 by Team17 for the Amiga and later in 1993 by MicroLeague for MS-DOS. The game is the first in the Alien Breed series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Alien_Breed_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Breed_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q965458"},{"title":"Breed","blocks":[{"text":"A breed is a specific group of breedable domestic animals having homogeneous appearance (phenotype), homogeneous behavior, and/or other characteristics that distinguish it from other organisms of the same species. In the literature, there exist several slightly deviating definitions. Breeds are formed through genetic isolation and either natural adaptation to the environment or selective breeding, or a combination of the two. Despite the centrality of the idea of \"breeds\" to animal husbandry and agriculture, no single, scientifically accepted definition of the term exists. A breed is therefore not an objective or biologically verifiable classification but is instead a term of art amongst groups of breeders who share a consensus around what qualities make some members of a given species members of a nameable subset."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Braunvieh_am_Simplonpass%2C_Schweiz.jpg/330px-Braunvieh_am_Simplonpass%2C_Schweiz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breed","wikidata":"Q38829"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ec/Alien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png/250px-Alien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ec/Alien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ec/Alien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png/250px-Alien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The flamethrower can be purchased with collected credits. On the top right is an Intex terminal, and two keys and an ammunition clip are scattered in the rooms on the right and above.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlien_Breed_Amiga_screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Viet